{
  "name": "Magic Item Tinker",
  "type": "feat",
  "_id": "lTGZZanCehoJePiS",
  "img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-star-orange.webp",
  "folder": "4RbdHSEXTHThnBoK",
  "sort": 400000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your Replicate Magic Item feature gains the following options.</p><p><strong>Charge Magic Item.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of you that you created with Replicate Magic Item and that uses charges. You expend a level 1+ spell slot and recharge the item: it regains a number of charges equal to the level of the slot.</p><p><strong>Drain Magic Item.</strong> As a Bonus Action, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of you that you created with Replicate Magic Item and make it vanish, converting its magic into a spell slot: level 1 if the item is Common, or level 2 if it is Uncommon or Rare. Once you use this option, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest. A slot created this way vanishes when you finish a Long Rest.</p><p><strong>Transmute Magic Item.</strong> As a Magic action, you can touch one magic item within 5 feet of you that you created with Replicate Magic Item and transform it into a different magic item based on a plan you know. Once you use this option, you can't do so again until you finish a Long Rest.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-coqT7P6xDFzm1k3D\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Charge Magic Item spends a spell slot (choose its level in the dialog) and the item regains that many charges. Drain Magic Item: add the level 1 or 2 slot to your spell slots yourself until your next Long Rest.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
